decisions:
  - id: tray-hide-on-close
    decision: Add a menu-bar tray and hide (not quit) the window on close
    rationale: The alarm scheduler is an in-app JS timer, so the process must stay alive for alarms to fire; hiding keeps the webview (and timers) running while giving a Show/Quit path.
  - id: duplicate-next-15
    decision: Duplicate an alarm to the next free 15-minute grid slot instead of an exact copy
    rationale: A duplicate sitting exactly on the original is useless; rounding up to the next unused :00/:15/:30/:45 makes duplication a fast way to build a series of alarms.
  - id: puzzle-dismiss-only
    decision: Puzzle gate blocks Dismiss only; Snooze stays free; sound pauses during solving with a 60s resume timeout and regenerating problems on wrong answers
    rationale: 'User wants to be forced awake without being trapped: solving is required to fully stop the alarm, but a stall or wrong guess brings the sound back so it can''t be silently abandoned, and snooze remains an easy ''not yet''.'
learnings:
  - A React countdown effect that depends on a parent-supplied callback restarts every render when the parent re-renders on a timer; hold the callback in a ref and run the interval effect once ([]).
  - Unmounting the media/beep player component is a clean way to pause alarm sound during the puzzle and auto-resume it on remount.
  - Tauri 2 tray needs the 'tray-icon' cargo feature; notifications need the notification plugin plus notification:default and core:window show/focus permissions in capabilities.
